{title: Little Basket on the River}
{subtitle: Exodus 2:1–10}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 60}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×11
| [C#] | [C#] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A#m]Three months I hid you in the [D#m]house
I could not hide you a[C#]ny more
[A#m]I made a basket out of [D#m]reeds
And [C#]laid you by the riv[D#m]er shore
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sleep, little [C#]one, on the [D#m]river
[C#]Sleep in the basket [D#m]of reeds
The Lord will [C#]watch you [D#m]on the water
Sleep, little one, [C#]sleep
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A#m]Your sister watches from a[D#m]far
To see what will be[C#]come of you
[A#m]The daughter of the king comes [D#m]down
She [C#]sees you crying, and [D#m]she knew
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sleep, little [C#]one, on the [D#m]river
[C#]Sleep in the basket [D#m]of reeds
The Lord will [C#]watch you [D#m]on the water
Sleep, little one, sleep
{end_of_chorus}
